WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.600
Order matters, because rules are tried
in order and the first match wins.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.346
The workbook's design guidance is
to put security advisories and

3
00:00:08.346 --> 00:00:12.300
retirements before the general rule
for anything that needs action.

4
00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:17.176
Here are the lab's six rules: security
to a security operations team at P2,

5
00:00:17.176 --> 00:00:21.722
retirements and maintenance to
cloud platform engineering at P3,

6
00:00:21.722 --> 00:00:26.102
incidents to the service desk at
P2, changes to cloud operations,

7
00:00:26.102 --> 00:00:29.325
and one rule that ignores
a Microsoft Viva post.

8
00:00:29.325 --> 00:00:32.189
Get the order wrong,
with a broad rule first,

9
00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:35.690
and security advisories
land in the general queue.
